cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use fstx, please cite it as below."
title: "fstx: Fast, Safe Column-Store Files for Python and R"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Chourasia
    given-names: Harsh
version: 1.2.0
date-released: 2026-11-28
license: MIT
url: "https://harshchourasia1.github.io/fstx/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/HarshChourasia1/fstx"
abstract: >-
  fstx is a column-store file format with one C++ engine under a Python package and an R package, so a file
  written from Python reads in R and the other way round. Every page gets the lightweight encoding that fits
  it (bit-packing, frame-of-reference, delta, run-length, dictionary, ALP for doubles, FSST for strings),
  optionally under ZSTD or LZ4, with a checksum per page; reads and writes run on all cores.
keywords:
  - columnar storage
  - file format
  - data frames
  - Apache Arrow
  - compression
  - Python
  - R
references:
  - type: article
    title: "ALP: Adaptive Lossless floating-Point Compression"
